      3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَآءَمْتُ بَيْنَ القَوْمِ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُلَآءَمَةٌ</span>, <i>I reconciled the people,</i> (S, Msb,) <i>and brought them
together.</i> (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَآءَمَهُ</span> <i>He was suited to him</i>
as a companion: see 5 in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زوى</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَآءَمَهُ</span>
<i>It</i> (food, T, and an affair, M) <i>suited him.</i> (T,
M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَا زَمَهُ</span>. (T.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  And <i>It coalesced,</i>
or <i>united, with it.</i>

